1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:08,154
A movie director is making a film
on the Tenpo famine,

2
00:00:08,238 --> 00:00:10,115
and they want to film
a peasant eating grass.

3
00:00:10,198 --> 00:00:11,324
A period movie!

4
00:00:11,407 --> 00:00:13,201
Konta, congratulations!

5
00:00:13,284 --> 00:00:16,079
-Congratulations!
-Konta! Congratulations!

6
00:00:16,871 --> 00:00:18,331
<i>Obon </i>holidays, huh.

7
00:00:18,414 --> 00:00:22,544
Shouldn't we at least visit Midori's
grandma's grave? She built this villa.

8
00:00:22,627 --> 00:00:24,712
-Grandma's photo!
-I want to see it!

9
00:00:25,588 --> 00:00:26,881
She was a beauty.

10
00:00:26,965 --> 00:00:28,299
I found a <i>yukata </i>in the storage room.

11
00:00:28,383 --> 00:00:30,260
Try it on.
Must be a keepsake from your grandma.

12
00:00:30,343 --> 00:00:34,722
-Ta-da!
-Oh! So cute!

13
00:00:34,806 --> 00:00:36,057
Summer festival?

14
00:00:36,141 --> 00:00:37,642
<i>Shall I guide you?</i>

15
00:00:37,725 --> 00:00:38,977
Wow.

16
00:00:39,686 --> 00:00:40,937
Could this be…

17
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:41,938
My Grandma's?

18
00:00:42,021 --> 00:00:44,732
Ms. Nobuko really loved this town.

19
00:00:44,816 --> 00:00:46,025
Can I take this back with me?

20
00:00:46,109 --> 00:00:46,943
It's <i>Obon</i>, after all.

21
00:00:47,026 --> 00:00:50,488
I think Grandma would be happier
if we kept them in the villa.

22
00:00:50,572 --> 00:00:53,950
<i>This way</i>
<i>Grandma can return to the villa too.</i>

23
00:00:54,784 --> 00:00:56,911
I'm glad I met you, Mr. Nishigami.

24
00:00:58,788 --> 00:01:01,708
<i>I'm home, Mr. Nishigami.</i>

25
00:01:08,965 --> 00:01:11,259
-So hot! Sorry Grandma!
-Hey, careful!

26
00:01:19,517 --> 00:01:21,394
Grandma, welcome back.

27
00:01:22,145 --> 00:01:25,982
Grandma, I think it's about time
I find success.

28
00:01:26,065 --> 00:01:27,817
So help me out!

29
00:01:27,901 --> 00:01:29,944
Make<i> The Great Tenpo Famine </i>a hit!

30
00:01:30,612 --> 00:01:32,196
Grandma, nice to meet you.

31
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:34,866
I'm Rinrin,
Midori's classmate from university.

32
00:01:34,949 --> 00:01:38,453
I have been feeling
very refreshed at your villa.

33
00:01:39,037 --> 00:01:41,414
Man, it really is a nice villa.

34
00:01:41,497 --> 00:01:45,209
I got to enjoy my vacation
while chipping away at my savings.

35
00:01:45,293 --> 00:01:48,213
We caught rainbow trout and ate them.

36
00:01:48,296 --> 00:01:50,423
Sorry for taking life from this land.

37
00:01:52,425 --> 00:01:56,012
Grandma,
thank you for leaving this villa behind.

38
00:01:56,554 --> 00:02:01,142
I lost my job, but thanks to this villa,

39
00:02:01,226 --> 00:02:03,561
I can have fun like this now.

40
00:02:04,896 --> 00:02:08,524
I think we siblings made you
worry a lot, but from now on,

41
00:02:08,608 --> 00:02:12,987
I will find my path
and move forward with all I have.

42
00:02:14,447 --> 00:02:17,158
-All right, let's eat.
-Yeah.

43
00:02:17,242 --> 00:02:18,952
Let's make an offering to Grandma too.

44
00:02:19,035 --> 00:02:20,536
-All right, let's drink!
-Yeah!

45
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:22,872
-I'll make some stupid alcohol for her.
-What?

46
00:02:23,831 --> 00:02:25,291
-It's fine.
-Regular alcohol is fine.

47
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:27,293
I think she would like my alcohol!

48
00:02:27,377 --> 00:02:30,004
No, that gives you a hangover.

49
00:02:30,088 --> 00:02:31,506
Do you want some, Grandma?

50
00:02:34,008 --> 00:02:35,843
It has been a while,

51
00:02:35,927 --> 00:02:37,136
Mr. Nishigami.

52
00:02:38,888 --> 00:02:41,557
Why are you here?

53
00:02:44,435 --> 00:02:47,730
At the end of summer,
a great flood will come,

54
00:02:48,481 --> 00:02:50,775
and there will be a landslide.

55
00:02:52,819 --> 00:02:53,987
Oh, dear!

56
00:02:55,321 --> 00:02:57,991
So, will they all die?

57
00:02:59,575 --> 00:03:01,536
They're still so young!

58
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:05,581
They haven't gotten
to live their lives yet, unlike me!

59
00:03:05,665 --> 00:03:08,167
There is nothing I can do.

60
00:03:10,211 --> 00:03:11,254
Please!

61
00:03:11,337 --> 00:03:13,256
Can't you save them?

62
00:03:14,173 --> 00:03:16,926
That is a grave violation of the rules.

63
00:03:19,929 --> 00:03:22,932
If you break the rules,
what will happen to you?

64
00:03:24,976 --> 00:03:29,105
It is impossible
for a Grim Reaper to break the rules.

65
00:03:30,648 --> 00:03:32,066
Goodness…

66
00:03:33,359 --> 00:03:34,318
Hey.

67
00:03:35,028 --> 00:03:39,741
If I try to change their destiny,

68
00:03:39,824 --> 00:03:43,244
will you be violating the rules
for telling me this?

69
00:03:45,496 --> 00:03:46,456
I don't know.

70
00:03:48,624 --> 00:03:50,418
There is no precedent.

71
00:04:37,882 --> 00:04:39,050
Hey, Midori.

72
00:04:39,133 --> 00:04:41,511
How was it with Mr. Nishigami?

73
00:04:41,594 --> 00:04:44,347
You've been acting weird
since you came back.

74
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:46,557
Could it be you two kissed?

75
00:04:46,641 --> 00:04:48,518
-No way!
-What are you talking about?

76
00:04:48,601 --> 00:04:50,061
We didn't!

77
00:04:50,144 --> 00:04:52,647
Then did you hold hands?

78
00:04:52,730 --> 00:04:53,898
-Huh?
-What?

79
00:04:53,981 --> 00:04:55,066
-Really?
-Who knows.

80
00:04:55,149 --> 00:04:56,734
Hey, you girls.

81
00:04:56,818 --> 00:04:58,736
This is no time to fool around.

82
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,697
You all must leave this place.

83
00:05:01,781 --> 00:05:03,991
You'll die in the typhoon!

84
00:05:05,284 --> 00:05:06,702
Did you really hold hands?

85
00:05:06,786 --> 00:05:07,745
No.

86
00:05:07,829 --> 00:05:09,330
Not exactly, but…

87
00:05:09,414 --> 00:05:11,541
But the vibes were good, right?

88
00:05:12,583 --> 00:05:14,001
What should I do?

89
00:05:14,085 --> 00:05:15,878
They can't hear me.

90
00:05:15,962 --> 00:05:17,588
Someone help!

91
00:05:17,672 --> 00:05:21,467
Please deliver my voice to these children!

92
00:05:21,968 --> 00:05:23,803
<i>Yes, I can hear you.</i>

93
00:05:25,763 --> 00:05:27,098
-Huh?
-What?

94
00:05:27,723 --> 00:05:28,766
Did it say something?

95
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:30,268
Wait.

96
00:05:30,351 --> 00:05:31,602
What is this?

97
00:05:31,686 --> 00:05:32,520
Hey.

98
00:05:33,479 --> 00:05:34,981
Hey, help me!

99
00:05:35,064 --> 00:05:36,190
<i>Yes!</i>

100
00:05:36,274 --> 00:05:38,317
<i>What kind of help do you need?</i>

101
00:05:38,401 --> 00:05:41,237
-The AI activated on its own?
-I wonder why?

102
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:43,364
Tell my grandchildren for me.

103
00:05:44,282 --> 00:05:46,617
<i>A message for your grandchildren?</i>

104
00:05:46,701 --> 00:05:48,244
-Yes!
-Grandchildren?

105
00:05:48,327 --> 00:05:49,871
We didn't say anything, though.

106
00:05:49,954 --> 00:05:51,664
-It must be broken.
<i>-Understood.</i>

107
00:05:51,747 --> 00:05:55,293
<i>I can repeat the sentences you say.</i>

108
00:05:55,376 --> 00:05:58,337
<i>What do you want me to repeat?</i>

109
00:05:59,964 --> 00:06:03,509
You are all grown adults,
yet you don't even work.

110
00:06:03,593 --> 00:06:04,927
You stay here every day,

111
00:06:05,011 --> 00:06:07,847
drinking alcohol,
just idling around in a place like this!

112
00:06:08,431 --> 00:06:11,893
<i>You are all grown adults, yet you</i>
<i>don't even work, you stay here every day,</i>

113
00:06:11,976 --> 00:06:14,228
<i>drinking alcohol, just idling around…</i>

114
00:06:14,312 --> 00:06:17,106
-Why does it know about our lives?
-So weird.

115
00:06:17,190 --> 00:06:18,524
In the first place,

116
00:06:18,608 --> 00:06:25,489
this villa isn't a place
for young people like you to come!

117
00:06:26,073 --> 00:06:28,701
<i>In the first place, a villa like this</i>

118
00:06:28,784 --> 00:06:32,330
<i>isn't a place</i>
<i>for young people like you to come!</i>

119
00:06:32,413 --> 00:06:37,501
This is a place for people who have
achieved a certain amount of success,

120
00:06:37,585 --> 00:06:41,589
and are semi-retired, to come to relax!

121
00:06:41,672 --> 00:06:44,300
<i>This is a place for people who have</i>

122
00:06:44,383 --> 00:06:49,597
<i>achieved a certain amount of success,</i>
<i>and are semi-retired, to come to relax!</i>

123
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:52,725
We want to succeed, but we can't!

124
00:06:52,808 --> 00:06:55,728
It will be okay!
You have<i> The Great Tenpo Famine </i>coming up!

125
00:06:55,811 --> 00:07:00,107
Go back to Tokyo right now!

126
00:07:00,191 --> 00:07:03,110
<i>Go back to Tokyo right now.</i>

127
00:07:03,194 --> 00:07:05,488
We won't go back now!

128
00:07:05,571 --> 00:07:07,156
We're on vacation!

129
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:08,616
Wow, so strict.

130
00:07:08,699 --> 00:07:12,787
I see, then I need a different approach.

131
00:07:13,287 --> 00:07:15,915
<i>I see, then I need a different approach.</i>

132
00:07:15,998 --> 00:07:17,500
What did it say?

133
00:07:19,377 --> 00:07:21,337
This villa

134
00:07:22,255 --> 00:07:24,131
is cursed!

135
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,300
If you stay here,

136
00:07:26,384 --> 00:07:31,138
all of you will die!

137
00:07:31,722 --> 00:07:34,267
<i>This villa is cursed.</i>

138
00:07:34,350 --> 00:07:37,520
<i>If you stay here, all of you will die!</i>

139
00:07:38,563 --> 00:07:41,357
Because, at the end of summer…

140
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:43,901
<i>Because, at the end of summer…</i>

141
00:07:44,443 --> 00:07:46,904
-What?
-A blackout?

142
00:07:47,446 --> 00:07:49,031
Did the breaker trip?

143
00:07:49,115 --> 00:07:50,950
Konta, go check the breaker.

144
00:07:51,033 --> 00:07:52,159
What is a breaker?

145
00:07:52,243 --> 00:07:53,536
-What?
-And where is it?

146
00:07:53,619 --> 00:07:57,248
I don't know, maybe over there?
In the hallway? Go look for it!

147
00:07:57,331 --> 00:07:58,624
I'm going.

148
00:07:58,708 --> 00:07:59,667
Well, it's fine.

149
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:03,087
Let's just make
a bonfire out there and drink.

150
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:06,257
No way! I'm scared when it's so dark!

151
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:09,218
-Konta, where are you? Come back!
-What's wrong, Rinrin?

152
00:08:09,302 --> 00:08:11,095
I'll look for a flashlight.

153
00:08:11,178 --> 00:08:12,263
-Hey!
-A flashlight?

154
00:08:12,346 --> 00:08:13,764
-Oh.
-Right.

155
00:08:15,808 --> 00:08:17,643
What's wrong?

156
00:08:17,727 --> 00:08:19,729
-You okay?
-What?

157
00:08:19,812 --> 00:08:22,023
I thought I saw your grandma's face.

158
00:08:22,106 --> 00:08:23,816
Hey, cut it out. Why say that?

159
00:08:23,899 --> 00:08:25,985
It looked like your grandma, Midori.

160
00:08:26,068 --> 00:08:28,404
-What?
-Just like the photo.

161
00:08:28,487 --> 00:08:32,158
-Cut it out, I'm scared!
-It's scary, isn't it?

162
00:08:33,492 --> 00:08:34,744
Oh, it's <i>Obon</i>!

163
00:08:34,827 --> 00:08:36,746
Grandma came to visit us!

164
00:08:40,916 --> 00:08:43,169
Grandma!

165
00:08:44,086 --> 00:08:45,004
Hey!

166
00:08:45,087 --> 00:08:47,423
Grandma, can you hear me?

167
00:08:47,506 --> 00:08:49,508
It's me, Midori.

168
00:08:51,385 --> 00:08:53,220
Grandma, you know,

169
00:08:54,138 --> 00:08:57,224
since coming to this villa,
I've been so happy.

170
00:08:57,308 --> 00:08:59,769
I've been enjoying the summer oranges
from the garden.

171
00:08:59,852 --> 00:09:01,354
I make them into juice!

172
00:09:01,437 --> 00:09:03,105
Mixed with alcohol, though.

173
00:09:03,189 --> 00:09:08,152
Grandma, this villa is dear to you,
so I will take care of it forever!

174
00:09:08,235 --> 00:09:10,529
Mr. Nishigami is here too, so it's fine.

175
00:09:11,113 --> 00:09:14,408
Next year, the year after next,
even when I become an adult…

176
00:09:14,492 --> 00:09:15,785
You are an adult, though.

177
00:09:16,369 --> 00:09:19,121
Even when I become a granny,
forever and ever.

178
00:09:19,205 --> 00:09:22,875
So that we can all spend
our vacations at this villa together.

179
00:09:50,319 --> 00:09:51,404
-Huh?
-What the heck?

180
00:09:57,410 --> 00:09:59,120
What are you two doing?

181
00:10:05,835 --> 00:10:08,129
I think what I did backfired.

182
00:10:08,713 --> 00:10:13,426
I thought if I pretended to be a ghost,
they would be scared and stay away.

183
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:16,929
But they…

184
00:10:17,012 --> 00:10:18,681
They know what I look like?

185
00:10:19,849 --> 00:10:20,975
It's <i>Obon</i>.

186
00:10:22,643 --> 00:10:26,981
They found old photos of you
and put them up around the house.

187
00:10:27,064 --> 00:10:28,065
So…

188
00:10:28,649 --> 00:10:29,650
I see.

189
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,237
That recognized me.

190
00:10:37,742 --> 00:10:40,202
You didn't mention the landslide, did you?

191
00:10:40,286 --> 00:10:41,829
I did!

192
00:10:41,912 --> 00:10:43,372
I said it,

193
00:10:43,456 --> 00:10:47,209
but that machine
didn't pick up those words.

194
00:10:47,793 --> 00:10:48,919
I see.

195
00:10:51,046 --> 00:10:53,466
Perhaps Lady Yomi intervened.

196
00:10:53,549 --> 00:10:54,884
Hey.

197
00:10:54,967 --> 00:10:56,635
Please, Mr. Nishigami.

198
00:10:56,719 --> 00:10:58,596
Save those children.

199
00:10:59,305 --> 00:11:01,515
They are still so young.

200
00:11:02,183 --> 00:11:05,728
And they have to die just because
they came here? It's a tragedy!

201
00:11:05,811 --> 00:11:09,231
When I meet them in heaven,
how do I even apologize…

202
00:11:09,315 --> 00:11:12,401
I cannot do as you requested.

203
00:11:14,069 --> 00:11:14,945
Wait.

204
00:11:15,029 --> 00:11:16,906
Please, Mr. Nishigami. Please.

205
00:11:16,989 --> 00:11:19,575
Let me talk with them!

206
00:11:20,242 --> 00:11:21,911
I cannot do that.

207
00:11:49,522 --> 00:11:51,649
<i>I am relieved, Grim Reaper.</i>

208
00:11:52,608 --> 00:11:56,946
<i>Lately, you have been playing around</i>
<i>with those humans almost every day,</i>

209
00:11:57,029 --> 00:11:58,614
<i>so I was worried.</i>

210
00:11:59,281 --> 00:12:02,952
<i>But it seems you understand</i>
<i>what your duties are.</i>

211
00:12:04,578 --> 00:12:05,788
Yes…

212
00:12:06,705 --> 00:12:10,459
<i>That old woman</i>
<i>lived out her natural lifespan,</i>

213
00:12:10,543 --> 00:12:13,587
<i>so she was able to come back for </i>Obon<i>.</i>

214
00:12:14,171 --> 00:12:16,006
<i>The lives of humans</i>

215
00:12:16,090 --> 00:12:20,511
<i>are built around comforting</i>
<i>the dead at every opportunity.</i>

216
00:12:24,098 --> 00:12:26,725
To comfort the dead…

217
00:12:28,018 --> 00:12:30,020
<i>Only in death is a human complete.</i>

218
00:12:30,604 --> 00:12:34,525
<i>With death, their lives are fulfilled.</i>

219
00:13:08,851 --> 00:13:10,019
Grandma…

220
00:13:13,063 --> 00:13:14,440
Thanks to you,

221
00:13:15,441 --> 00:13:16,442
I may…

222
00:13:19,194 --> 00:13:22,114
be falling in love for the first time!

223
00:13:27,453 --> 00:13:29,622
<i>As the </i>Obon <i>holiday comes to an end,</i>

224
00:13:29,705 --> 00:13:33,459
<i>people are rushing back</i>
<i>from hometowns and tourist destinations.</i>

225
00:13:34,168 --> 00:13:35,377
<i>On expressways,</i>

226
00:13:35,461 --> 00:13:39,715
<i>heavy congestion has been occurring</i>
<i>since morning, mainly on inbound lines,</i>

227
00:13:39,798 --> 00:13:44,136
<i>with long lines of cars</i>
<i>even exceeding 30 to 40 kilometers.</i>

228
00:13:46,388 --> 00:13:48,223
HATO SABLÉS!

229
00:14:17,670 --> 00:14:19,004
This person…

230
00:14:21,173 --> 00:14:22,216
Who is this?

231
00:14:36,939 --> 00:14:38,107
Thank you.

232
00:14:43,946 --> 00:14:45,114
<i>Now to our next story.</i>

233
00:14:45,864 --> 00:14:47,866
<i>From now until the end of summer,</i>

234
00:14:47,950 --> 00:14:52,121
<i>there will be increased risk</i>
<i>of powerful typhoons forming.</i>

235
00:14:52,705 --> 00:14:54,331
<i>According to the Meteorological Agency…</i>

236
00:15:28,824 --> 00:15:30,534
<i>Orange peels…</i>

237
00:15:30,617 --> 00:15:32,161
<i>How do you make them?</i>

238
00:15:32,244 --> 00:15:33,912
<i>If you want, we can make them together.</i>

239
00:15:33,996 --> 00:15:35,581
Konta. I'm going with you.

240
00:15:35,664 --> 00:15:36,540
Tetsuro!

241
00:15:36,623 --> 00:15:38,250
I'm going to fish for horse mackerel.

242
00:15:38,333 --> 00:15:40,335
You got the first fish!

243
00:15:40,419 --> 00:15:44,715
In order to survive,
you even have to eat grass!

244
00:15:44,798 --> 00:15:46,633
You're interested in Midori, aren't you?

245
00:15:47,342 --> 00:15:49,136
<i>Am I?</i>

246
00:15:49,219 --> 00:15:50,596
<i>Hey, so…</i>

247
00:15:50,679 --> 00:15:53,307
What is our relationship right now?

248
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:56,351
<i>Your recent actions</i>
<i>have been unacceptable.</i>

249
00:15:56,435 --> 00:15:59,605
<i>Falling in love with a human</i>
<i>is out of the question.</i>

250
00:15:59,688 --> 00:16:03,776
